        "original_id": "ea0d558d-edfd-563f-bd6c-0c20b82a37eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Cocteau\n- Works: La Machine à écrire, Les Enfants Terribles, The Blood of a Poet, Beauty and the Beast, Les Parents Terribles, Orpheus\n- Places: Paris, Théâtre Hébertot\n- Roles: writer, designer, playwright, artist, filmmaker, dramatist\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Maurice Eugène Clément Cocteau was born on 5 July 1889 and died on 11 October 1963.\n- Jean Cocteau was a French writer, designer, playwright, artist, filmmaker, and dramatist.\n- Jean Cocteau is best known for the novel Les Enfants Terribles, published in 1929.\n- Jean Cocteau is best known for the film The Blood of a Poet, released in 1930.\n- La Machine à écrire is a three-act play written by French dramatist Jean Cocteau.\n- La Machine à écrire premiered on 29 April 1941 at the Théâtre Hébertot in Paris.\n- Jean Cocteau is best known for the film Beauty and the Beast, released in 1946.\n- Jean Cocteau is best known for the film Les Parents Terribles, released in 1948.\n- Jean Cocteau is best known for the film Orpheus, released in 1949.",
